# T42 (packet 024): everything live/local/generated/secret stays OUT of the repo - nothing here is a
# judgment call made once and forgotten; `tests/test_repo_hygiene.py` re-checks the tracked set itself for
# a stray secret/absolute-path on every test run, so a future addition that violates this file's own
# intent fails loudly instead of silently landing in a commit. A pattern with no leading slash already
# matches at ANY depth (git's own documented behavior), so entries below are listed once, not duplicated
# per directory level.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python -------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Node / Next.js / Playwright -----------------
node_modules/
.next/
# T48: the previous build, renamed out of the way so `next build` gets a clean dir (the sandbox's
# bulk-delete guard blocks emptying .next in one go). Harmless to delete by hand at any time.
.next-old/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- live data / embedded Postgres / raw crawls --
# The live, real data dir (the host's own $HOME/.ajp/, per README.md's own "ajp-init" section) is OUTSIDE
# this repo entirely, never reachable by a commit from in here. These are the project's own LOCAL/dev-time
# equivalents (tools/dev_up.py's own temp stack, any ad-hoc local data dir) - never committed either, for
# the exact same reason: real crawled content, embedded-Postgres binary files, and anything derived from a
# live run has no business in version control.
data/
raw/
raw_pdf/
pgdata/
*.log
logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- uploaded applicant/thesis files -------------
# D4/Privacy page: an uploaded CV or thesis file is analysed locally and never sent anywhere else - "never
# committed to a public git history" is the exact same promise, extended to this repo's own history. This
# is the RUNTIME upload storage location specifically (ajp.applicants.store/ajp.thesis.store's own default
# root, already covered by `data/` above since both live under it by default) - spelled out explicitly in
# case either default root is ever overridden to somewhere else under the repo. Deliberately NOT a blanket
# `*.pdf`/`*.docx` rule, which would also exclude this project's own committed, intentional test fixtures
# (tests/cv_fixtures/, tests/thesis_fixtures/, tests/fixtures/documents/ - real .docx/.pdf files the test
# suite itself depends on being tracked).
data/applicants/
data/thesis/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets / environment ------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!web/.env.local.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OS / editor noise -----------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
